## Context
Celebrate sweep after raid 188-193. Ticket 0193 fixed `erg version`'s outdated-binary
hint to say "see README" instead of `make install-erg-binary`. The same contributor-only
reference appears in `src/go/assets/integration.md` line 74 (Uninstall section):

```
If you installed erg to `~/.local/bin` via `make install-erg-binary`,
also remove that copy:
```

A regular user who installed via curl has no `~/.local/bin/erg` copy (that path is
created only by `make install-erg-binary`, which requires a source checkout). The
sentence is accurate but references a contributor-only workflow — a non-contributor
reading the uninstall section will be confused.

Same class as 0193: contributor-facing make target exposed to end-user docs.

## Actions
1. Edit `src/go/assets/integration.md` (canonical embedded copy) Uninstall section.
2. Rephrase line 74 to clarify this only applies to contributor installs:
   "If you copied erg to `~/.local/bin` manually (e.g. via `make install-erg-binary`
   if you have a source checkout), also remove that copy:"
   Or simply remove the `make install-erg-binary` reference entirely since a
   curl-install user never creates that path.
3. Validate: `tickets/erg validate tickets/0196-*.erg`
4. Run: `make check-fast`

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `src/go/assets/integration.md` Uninstall section no longer exposes
      `make install-erg-binary` to non-contributor readers as a required step,
      OR clarifies it is a contributor-only path
